\details{
For this engine, there is a single mode: classification
\subsection{Tuning Parameters}{

This model has 3 tuning parameters:
\itemize{
\item \code{ordinal_link}: Ordinal Link (type: character, default: logit)
\item \code{threshold_structure}: Threshold Structure (type: character, default:
flexible)
\item \code{parallel_reg}: Parallel Regression (type: logical, default: TRUE)
}

\code{ordinal_link} is translated to the native \code{link} argument. In addition
to the standard links, this engine supports \code{"Aranda-Ordaz"} and
\code{"log-gamma"}. The dial value \code{"logistic"} is translated to the native
value \code{"logit"}.

\code{threshold_structure} is translated to the native \code{threshold} argument.
Its values are \code{"flexible"}, \code{"symmetric_median"}, \code{"symmetric_zero"},
and \code{"equidistant"}, which map to the native values \code{"flexible"},
\code{"symmetric"}, \code{"symmetric2"}, and \code{"equidistant"}, respectively.

\code{parallel_reg = FALSE} puts every predictor in the native \code{nominal}
formula and leaves an intercept-only \code{location} formula; at least one
predictor is required. The native \code{nominal} argument can be passed
through \code{\link[=set_engine]{set_engine()}} only when \code{parallel_reg} is not
set.
}

